    <string name="tvclient_local_title">Home network</string>
    <string name="tvclient_local_edit">Home network address …</string>
    <string name="tvclient_local_hint">At home, Quallenkino talks to the server directly (faster than over the internet). The address only applies in the network where it was saved – elsewhere the normal address is used. Your sign-in stays the same. Recommended: use https if possible – over http the access token can be read by others on the home network.</string>
    <string name="tvclient_local_dialog">Local address of the server, e.g. its IP in your home network. Without a port, 8096 is used. “Save” confirms the address for the network the device is in right now. Leave empty or choose “Remove” to use only the normal address. If the home address stops working (e.g. after reinstalling the plugin on the server), saving it again helps.</string>
    <string name="tvclient_local_example">e.g. 192.168.1.10:8096</string>
